<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Venlo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Venlo is a city in the province of Limburg in the south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> close to the German border. A member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a> in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, it was a fortified river town contested in the wars of the 16th to 18th centuries. It was confirmed as part of the Netherlands in 1839 and is today a centre of logistics and horticulture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/venlo.jpg" alt="Venlo" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: giggel · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Venlo_%E2%80%93_Parade_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
